<p>Iranian human rights activist and 2023 Nobel Peace Prize laureate Narges Mohammadi was transferred to a Tehran hospital on Sunday, May 10, after a medical crisis that began in Zanjan prison, her foundation said. The foundation said the transfer followed days of appeals by her family and supporters, who described her condition as critical. The foundation said Iranian authorities suspended Mohammadi’s prison sentence on heavy bail, without disclosing the amount or how long the suspension would last. Supporters said she had spent about 10 days in a Zanjan hospital before being taken by ambulance to Tehran so her own medical team could treat her. Mohammadi, 54, had been held in Zanjan prison since December and has spent much of the past two decades in and out of Iranian custody over her activism. She received the 2023 Nobel Peace Prize for her work against the oppression of women in Iran and for human rights and freedom, according to the Nobel citation cited in several reports.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/AInwcmznyI_zst1jbpJBTUz8VW2PyWIoxGPYFZy1kAWQyCHD_3QWDv6BLRLvL_qM7PpoV-09LLTCz9zqIy65ZDNZMdLYw0Y-_c77flU2dxmFPa319g-x4PA1Um_J9shH28uCFnGAUadPOsqbsi14NJbI272Hu-5e-PheGbJ3d00PZIhpBVqJXKVNp7sBhmaPHZXZf51AjVAEkbcJY6PfX4dx5C-60jAmYyznRdrLU-UesSS3f4HgbBXJw5Tif9ndLTZ3' alt='Narges Mohammadi.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Health claims: Supporters said Mohammadi suffered two suspected heart attacks behind bars, while her lawyers said she had lost about 20 kilograms and was “unrecognisable” compared with before her latest arrest.</li><li>Reported charge: One report said the case underlying her latest imprisonment involved alleged propaganda against the regime.</li><li>International pressure: Reports described weeks of mounting international pressure as concerns about her condition grew.</li><li>Remaining term: Her foundation said she still faces 18 years in prison.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Narges Mohammadi Foundation: The foundation said a bail-based sentence suspension was insufficient and that Mohammadi needs permanent, specialized medical care. (<a href='https://tg24.sky.it/mondo/2026/05/10/iran-narges-mohammadi-ricovero-ospedale'>Sky TG24</a>)</li><li>Mostafa Nili: Mohammadi’s lawyer said Iran’s Legal Medicine Organization found that she needed specialized treatment outside prison because of multiple medical conditions. (<a href='https://veja.abril.com.br/mundo/nobel-da-paz-narges-mohammadi-deixa-prisao-no-ira-para-tratamento-medico/'>Veja</a>)</li><li>Family and supporters: Mohammadi’s relatives and colleagues called for her full release and the dismissal of charges after the temporary bail decision. (<a href='https://kurir.mk/vesti/svet/nobelovkata-narges-mohamadi-e-prefrlena-vo-bolnitsa-vo-teheran/'>Kurir</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/middle-east/article/3353072/jailed-iran-nobel-laureate-narges-mohammadi-transferred-hospital-after-medical-crisis'>Jailed Iran Nobel laureate Narges Mohammadi transferred to hospital after medical crisis</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/middle-east/jailed-iranian-peace-laureate-mohammadi-moved-to-hospital-in-tehran'>Jailed Iranian peace laureate Mohammadi moved to hospital in Tehran</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://abcnews.com/International/wireStory/nobel-laureate-narges-mohammadi-transferred-tehran-hospital-foundation-132830360'>Nobel laureate Narges Mohammadi is transferred to a Tehran hospital, her foundation says</a> - abcnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/nobel-laureate-narges-mohammadi-transferred-to-a-tehran-hospital-her-foundation-says/article70964216.ece'>Nobel laureate Narges Mohammadi transferred to a Tehran hospital, her foundation says</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c1j257w87neo'>Ailing Iran Nobel laureate given bail and hospital transfer</a> - bbc.com</li><li><a href='https://www.al-